[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-6
TITLE: Functional1
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control Bootloader firmware shall jump to execution of the main application if and only if the existing main application code at startup
is valid. The main application code is valid if the programmed CRC value matches the application firmware loaded in flash memory.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power
2. Don’t load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the Bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory but terminate the PC utility partway through.
4. Power cycle the system
5. Load a treatment plan
6. Run the loaded treatment.
7. While keeping power on, load the application firmware once more to completion from the flash memory.
8. Power cycle the system
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is started up successfully
2. The system doesn’t have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. The system is off
4. The system is started up successfully
5. The plan is loaded successfully
6. The application is loaded successfully
7. Verify the treatment plan cannot be executed.
8. The system is powered up successfully and the loaded treatment can now be performed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-8
TITLE: Functional 2
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall be able to write a specified flash memory page with provided data from the PC.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power
2. Don’t load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the Bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory but terminate the PC utility partway through.
4. Record the utility log to ensure the application writes data to flash memory
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is started up successfully
2. The system doesn’t have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. The system is off
4. The system is started up successfully
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-9
TITLE: Functional 3
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash memory corresponding to the application firmware programming area.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power
2. Don’t load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the Bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory
4. Record the utility log to ensure the application erases MCU memory
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system is starting successfully
2. The system doesn’t have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. The new firmware application is loaded successfully
4. Record the utility log to ensure the application erases MCU memory
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-4
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-10
TITLE: PC Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control Bootloader firmware shall be able to respond to a ping command from the PC, indicating that the system is in Bootloader mode.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power
2. Don’t load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the Bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory.
4. Record the utility log to ensure application enters Bootloader mode
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify System is start up successfully
2. Verify System doesn’t have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the new firmware application is loaded successfully
4. Verify application enters Bootloader mode
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-5
  ROLE: Verifies

